Subject: [PATCH] a dismount settle keeps its falling flags and has a bound

WHY THIS PATCH EXISTS

Two defects in CheckMountStateAction::CompleteDismount, the path that fires on
every SMSG_DISMOUNT.

1. It cleared MOVEMENTFLAG_FALLING two lines after MotionMaster::MoveFall set
it, under the running spline, so a connected client was told it was not falling
during the descent whose landing packet Player::HandleFall bills. Keeping the
flag needs two things. The signal is the spline itself (not Finalized and
isFalling), because the flag reads the same before and after for a bot already
falling, and MoveFall sets it before a launch that can fail. And something must
clear it at the end: EffectMovementGenerator::Finalize returns before its flag
clear for a player (PointMovementGenerator.cpp:371) and a bot with no client
sends no MSG_MOVE_FALL_LAND. Left on, the flag sends PathGenerator straight down
(PathGenerator.cpp:325) and freezes the fall baseline in PlayerbotAI::UpdateAI.
TempestKeepStuckFallingTrigger is that same stuck flag, on one map. So
CompleteDismount now returns whether a fall spline is running, and
PlayerbotAI::FinishDismountDescent clears the flags from the AI tick once that
recorded spline has finished. A client's own fall is never recorded, so its
flag stays with its packets.

2. MoveFall searches with MAX_FALL_DISTANCE, 250000.0f, and the comment above
the call once called that a guard. Where nothing lies within 50 yards it finds a
surface arbitrarily far down and commits to the whole descent. A 50 yard drop is
at most 65.7% of maximum health at Rate.Damage.Fall = 1, and 69.03 yards is one
kill from full health, so DEFAULT_HEIGHT_SEARCH is also the distance that keeps
one settle from being lethal. MoveFall is left unbounded for a bot with a flight
flag: a flyer forced down at Dalaran really is in the air.

The bound rests on magnitude. The fall death capture the ticket asks for is
still to come, and a settle refused here logs at DEBUG on the playerbots channel.

WHAT WOULD LET THIS PATCH BE DELETED

Upstream mod-playerbots bounding the dismount settle and keeping the falling
flags under a running fall spline, with a landing clear for a bot with no
client.

APPLIES TO

quadseven/mod-playerbots @ 40884e9c135c1daf27ffd894a6047502a5701130, on top of
local patches 0001-0018. Touches CompleteDismount, PlayerbotAI::UpdateAI and the
SMSG_DISMOUNT case. tests/replay_dismount_fall.py runs the patched and pinned
code through the same scenarios for both deployments.

